{
  "description": "Language-agnostic laws of the brep.feature widgets. Every case names a catalogue kind, its inputs (shape recipes, selections by plane normal, edge ends, curved faces or stale labels, plain numbers) and either the expected outputs or the expected fault. Shape outputs state their analytic kind, volume, area and bounds, derived by hand in the case names' formulas: a straight edge strip removes (1 - pi/4) r^2 per unit length, a chamfer prism d^2/2, the all-edge chamfer is the cube clipped by twelve half-spaces. Rust runs the fixture against the kernel and the pinned tessellations; the TypeScript oracle recomputes volume, area, bounds and closedness of every pinned mesh with three.",
